Constructors is the Spcial Methods to declare the objects 

there are three Important rules for constructor
i) Constructors name will always be the same as class Name.
ii) Constructors can't have Return type.
iii) Constructors can automatically called when object is created.

Types of Constructors

i) Default Constructors;
ii) Parameterized Constructor
iii) No-Arugument Constructor


example code

class Book{
String Name;
double price;
Book(){
System.out.println("Default Constructor");
 }

Book(String Name,double price){
    this.Name=Name;
    this.price=price;
}
void display(){
System.out.println("Name: "+Name+"\n"+"price: "+price);
}
}
public class Main{
public static void main(String[] args){
Book b=new Book();
Book b1=new Book("The new Beginning",34560);
 b1.display();
}
}
